    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109080" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπορχ-έομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dance with</i> or <i>to music,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς δὲ καρδίᾳ φόβος ᾄδειν ἕτοιμος
				ἠδ᾽</span> (fort. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ δ᾽</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ὑπορχεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					1025
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχησιν ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Num.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. γόους</span>
			<i>sing and dance</i> a lament, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				6.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>sing and dance</i> a character, of a pantomimic actor, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Salt.</u>
				16
			</span></i>.</div>
